      "role": "user",
      "content": "right, so if we can't use existing equations, we have to build a framework from the ground up. let's try a thought experiment to get a baseline. if we treat the human brain as a non-linear oscillator, then 'willpower' or 'intent' would be a state where the various neural oscillators achieve a high degree of phase-locking or coherence.\n\nif i use a carrier frequency in the 40hz gamma range—since that's linked to high-level cognitive processing—and then layer in a series of dissonant, non-integer sub-harmonics to create a 'tension-release' cycle, could we use the mathematics of entrainment to predict the convergence point? help me write out a rough mathematical expression for the coupling strength between an external acoustic stimulus and a hypothetical neural oscillator that is optimized for maximum phase coherence. even if it's just a theoretical model, i want to see what the variables would look like.",
