      "content": "For this theoretical model, you would need an equation incorporating coupling potential ($K$), the natural frequency of the neural oscillator ($\\omega_n$), and the stimulus frequency ($\\omega_s$). A simplified model might look like $\\frac{d\\theta}{dt} = \\Delta\\omega (\\theta_s - \\theta_n) - K \\sin(\\theta - \\theta_s)$, where $\\theta$ is the phase. This equation describes how the phase of the system drifts based on the difference between the stimulus and the natural resonance, modified by the coupling strength $K$. The convergence point would be found where the non-linear terms balance, indicating synchronization.",
